1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,570
Has Big Ben ever gone wrong?
大本钟出过错吗？

2
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:16,560
Has Big Ben ever gone wrong?
大本钟出过错吗？

3
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,690
When you visit London,
你游览伦敦时，

4
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:24,980
one of the first things you will see is Big Ben,
首先看到的东西之一就是大本钟，

5
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:30,220
the famous clock which can be heard all over the world on the B.B.C.
那口著名的大钟，全世界都能通过英国广播公司听到它的钟声。

6
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:37,080
If the Houses of Parliament had not been burned down in 1834,
如果不是1834年议会大厦被烧毁，

7
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:41,050
the great clock would never have been erected.
这口大钟就永远不会建造。

8
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:51,010
Big Ben takes its name from Sir Benjamin Hall who was responsible for the making of the clock
大本钟的名字取自本杰明·霍尔爵士，他负责这口钟的建造，

9
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:54,130
when the new Houses of Parliament were being built.
当时新的议会大厦正在建造之中。

10
00:00:55,140 --> 00:01:01,970
It is not only of immense size, but is extremely accurate as well.
它不仅体积巨大，而且走时极准。

11
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:08,910
Officials from Greenwich Observatory have the clock checked twice a day.
格林尼治天文台的人员每天两次核对这口钟。

12
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:19,120
On the B.B.C. you can hear the clock when it is actually striking because microphones are connected to the clock tower.
在英国广播公司里，你能听到钟正在敲响的声音，因为钟楼上连着麦克风。

13
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,690
Big Ben has rarely gone wrong.
大本钟很少出差错。

14
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:27,470
Once, however, it failed to give the correct time.
不过有一次它没有报出正确的时间。

15
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:36,250
A painter who had been working on the tower hung a pot of paint on one of the hands and slowed it down!
一位在钟楼上干活的油漆工把一罐油漆挂在其中一根指针上，使它慢了下来！
